course: dictionary
lesson: 2317
title: A weapon in context
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A crossbow is a weapon, and the words around it tell you what it is. In history lessons about the Middle Ages, crossbows were powerful and easy to learn, «compared with longbows». The word compared shows that a crossbow is being set against another kind of bow.
explain: Look for clues in the words after it. «Crossbow bolt» is a phrase that tells you a bolt is something a crossbow shoots, and a crossbow is a kind of bow, so a bolt is probably a kind of arrow. You can check this: a bolt is a short arrow shot from a crossbow.
explain: Some sentences tell you when something happened. «Crossbows by the 5th century BC» means they are very old, and «ancient Greece had its own early forms of both» means Greece had earlier versions of the same weapon. Early forms are not the crossbow you see in stories, but the idea behind it.
fact: A crossbow is a weapon made of a small bow fixed across a wooden stock.
fact: When you pull the trigger, a crossbow shoots short arrows called bolts.
fact: «Crossbow bolt» means the short arrow that a crossbow fires.
fact: In the Middle Ages, crossbows were powerful and easy to learn compared with longbows.
fact: Crossbows are very old: «Crossbows by the 5th century BC» shows they existed a very long time ago.
exercise: What does a crossbow do when you pull its trigger? | Opens a door | Sings a song | Glows in the dark | *Shoots a short arrow called a bolt
exercise: «The crossbow was powerful and easy to learn, unlike the longbow.» What does powerful mean? | Quiet, like a whisper | Weak and slow | Pretty and decorated | *Strong, able to shoot hard
exercise: «Ancient Greece had its own early forms of the crossbow.» What does early forms mean? | *Earlier versions | Painted decorations | Copies bought from shops | Newer models
test: «Some things, like the crossbow, were invented in more than one place.» What does invented mean? | Lost forever | *Made or created for the first time | Broken into pieces | Bought in a shop
test: What is a crossbow bolt? | *A short arrow shot from a crossbow | A wooden stock | A kind of trigger | A stone wall of a medieval castle
exam: What does «fire a crossbow» mean? | Paint it red | Carry it to school | *Shoot it, so a bolt flies out | Light it with a match
